<%# A theme's own Diagram block, written from what `Theme::Contract` gives the template (`block`, `page`,
    `svg`, `description`, `caption`; docs/reference/theming.md, "The Diagram block"): the drawing printed as
    given in a box that scrolls, which is a keyboard stop named by the description, and the caption through
    ERB's own escaping. %>
<div class="plain-diagram" data-block="<%= block.id %>" data-page="<%= page.id %>">
  <div class="plain-diagram__drawing" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="<%= description %>"><%= svg %></div>
  <% if caption.present? %><p class="plain-diagram__caption"><%= caption %></p><% end %>
</div>
